  "text": {
    "paragraphs": [
      "This is my street. My name is Sam. I am eight. I live in the blue house. Three children live close to me. I draw them with my crayons. Dad looks at my picture. \"Who is this?\" asks Dad.",
      "This is Ann. She is ten. She has a yellow bike. She is a good friend. This is Mark. He is six. He has a red kite. \"Is Mark five?\" asks Dad. \"No, that is not correct,\" I say. \"Mark is six.\"",
      "This is Eva. She is three. She is a small child. Her house is next to my house. Eva likes my crayons. I give her a blue crayon. \"Thank you, Sam!\" says Eva. Now I have three friends on my street. I like my street."
    ],
    "summary": "Sam draws the three children who live close to him. He tells Dad the name and age of each child, and he gives Eva a crayon.",
